                            "fullDescription": {
                                "text": "A LinearLayout which contains an ImageView and a TextView can be more efficiently handled as a compound drawable (a single TextView, using the drawableTop, drawableLeft, drawableRight and/or drawableBottom attributes to draw one or more images adjacent to the text).\n\nIf the two widgets are offset from each other with margins, this can be replaced with a drawablePadding attribute.\n\nThere's a lint quickfix to perform this conversion in the Eclipse plugin.",
                                "markdown": "A `LinearLayout` which contains an `ImageView` and a `TextView` can be more efficiently handled as a compound drawable (a single TextView, using the `drawableTop`, `drawableLeft`, `drawableRight` and/or `drawableBottom` attributes to draw one or more images adjacent to the text).\n\nIf the two widgets are offset from each other with margins, this can be replaced with a `drawablePadding` attribute.\n\nThere's a lint quickfix to perform this conversion in the Eclipse plugin."
